concept:
Reusable logic keeps programs clean. IEC / Siemens SCL text uses two forms:

    FUNCTION (FC)        -- stateless; returns a value; no memory between calls
    FUNCTION_BLOCK (FB)  -- has memory (an instance); e.g. a timer, a motor FB

A FUNCTION assigns its result to its own name and closes with END_FUNCTION:

    FUNCTION ClampHigh : REAL
    VAR_INPUT
        IN : REAL;
        HI : REAL;
    END_VAR
        IF IN > HI THEN
            ClampHigh := HI;
        ELSE
            ClampHigh := IN;
        END_IF;
    END_FUNCTION

solution:
(* Lesson 08 -- Functions & Function Blocks (Reusable Logic) *)
(* Write a FUNCTION ClampHigh : REAL that limits IN so it never exceeds HI.  *)
(* (Pure math here -- no field contacts, so no XIC/XIO.)                     *)

FUNCTION ClampHigh : REAL
VAR_INPUT
    IN : REAL;
    HI : REAL;
END_VAR
(* ----- YOUR LOGIC : write your answer between these two lines ----- *)
    IF IN > HI THEN
        ClampHigh := HI;
    ELSE
        ClampHigh := IN;
    END_IF;
(* ------------------------------------------------------------------ *)
END_FUNCTION
